# Ooda CLI — Environment Variables

File: ooda/docs/env.oot

The `ooda` binary reads 11 environment variables. Each is consumed in exactly one or two files; this file is the single place that lists them all, their defaults, and their consumers. Vars are grouped by who sets them (install step vs host vs user).

## Set by the install step (post-condition)

The install command writes `$OODA_HOME/.config/ooda/env`. Editors and shells should `source` it. The 5 vars below are exported there.

### OODA_HOME

The ooda install root. Default: `$HOME/.local/share/ooda`. Written by `cli/build/install.oo` as `ooda_home`. Not used to find oodac.

### OODA_SRC_ROOT

The source tree root. Default: same as `OODA_HOME`. Written by install. Not used to find oodac.

### OODA_STD

The stdlib path. Default: `$OODA_HOME/std`. Set so the compiler and runtime can find `std/result.oo`, `std/fs/path.oo`, etc.

### OODA_CONFIG

The config dir. Default: `$HOME/.config/ooda`. Holds the `env` file that exports this group.

### OODA_CACHE

The cache dir. Default: `$HOME/.cache/ooda`. Used by `test` for per-invocation artifacts (`.ooda-cache/test/test-<ms>.oo.bin`) and by the reproducible-build CAS.

## Set by the user (optional, override defaults)

These override the install-step defaults. None are required for normal use, but they are how you point ooda at a non-standard layout.

### OODACODEX

Required dir for spawned binaries. Consumed by `build/spawn.oo::spawn()`. `OODA_CODEX` is an alias. The spawn path is `$codex/bin/<name>`. Unset, empty, unsafe name, or missing bin fails closed. No `$PATH` lookup.

### OODA_COMPILER

Required path to the oodac binary. Consumed by `find_oodac`. The only compiler locator. Unset, empty, missing, or a basename of `ooda` fails closed.

### OODA_FS_WRITEDIR

Required by `ooda install`. Consumed by `cli/build/install.oo::require_writedir`. Refuses to run when unset. Refuses any `--to` path that is not under this writedir. Acts as the install-time safety gate.

### OODA_CHECKOUT

Fallback for `ooda install --from`. Consumed by `cli/build/install.oo` when `--from` is not given. Defaults to `.` (current dir).

### OODA_VERSION

Optional version string written into the install receipt. Consumed by `cli/build/install.oo` as `version=...` in `INSTALL_RECEIPT.txt`. Defaults to `v0.2.16` when unset.

### OODA_INSTALLER

Optional local installer script for `ooda update`. Consumed by `cli/build/update.oo` when `--installer` is not given. Falls back to the canonical `https://openooda.org/install.sh` URL when unset or empty. Must pass the same safe-path gate as `--installer`.

## Lookup for oodac

`find_oodac` (in `cli/build/find_compiler.oo`) prefers `OODA_COMPILER`, then `OODA_TOOLCHAIN/bin/oodac`, then `HOME/.openooda/bin/oodac`. The path must exist and must not have basename `ooda`. Else print `ERR\tcli\tno oodac at OODA_COMPILER` or `ERR\tcli\tno oodac (OODA_COMPILER, OODA_TOOLCHAIN, or HOME layout)` and exit 1.

## Lookup for opm, lsp, mcp (spawned)

`build/spawn.oo::spawn()` reads `OODA_CODEX` or `OODACODEX`. The bin is `$codex/bin/<name>`. The name must not contain `/` or `..`. The file must exist. Else spawn returns Err.

## What ooda does NOT read

- `OODA_REPO_ROOT` — the legacy root var; not consumed by this version.
- `OODA_LOG_LEVEL` — there is no log-level switch; ooda prints what it prints.
- `OODA_CONFIG_FILE` — there is no JSON or TOML config; all config is env vars + argv.
- `OODA_PROFILE` — no profile switch.

If you set one of these, ooda ignores it silently.
